            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Union Pacific Railroad, the dispute centers on the Railway Labor Act\u2019s Section\u202f3\u202fFirst\u202f(q), which makes division awards conclusive except for three expressly listed exceptions."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Union Pacific Railroad",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Union Pacific Railroad, union Pacific argues that the respondent waived the first statutory ground of review in its brief to the Seventh Circuit."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Union Pacific Railroad",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 14,
              "start": 14
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Union Pacific Railroad, union Pacific contends that the statute guarantees specific procedural rights, not an abstract notion of fairness."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Respondent",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 56,
              "start": 56
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The respondent maintains that the Steelworker trilogy standard for labor arbitration does not apply under the Railway Labor Act."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Mr. Ballenger",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "f7c5ac7d273cf5b4f22d4217d2d8c5c4cd80379f782675713b0042bb656151b1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-f7c5ac7d273c-0001-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 22,
              "start": 22
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Mr. Ballenger, the respondent argues that evidence of conferencing is essential to the board\u2019s consideration of disputes, citing a 40\u2011year\u2011old precedent (Award\u202f18679)."
      }
    ],
